  ["mage-frost.s3.low3.if"] = "between fights, when the bar is low",
  ["mage-frost.s3.low3.text"] = "Sit and drink",
  ["mage-frost.s3.low3.why"] = "a full bar buys the next pulls",
  ["mage-frost.s3.opening1.if"] = "Frost, Ice from 30, or Mage from 34 for mana",
  ["mage-frost.s3.opening1.text"] = "An armour",
  ["mage-frost.s3.opening1.why"] = "armour keeps you alive, and Mage Armor gives mana",
  ["mage-frost.s3.opening2.if"] = "once, before the first pull",
  ["mage-frost.s3.opening2.why"] = "more Intellect means more mana to cast with",
  ["mage-frost.s3.opening3.if"] = "from as far as you can reach",
  ["mage-frost.s3.opening3.why"] = "it is your main bolt, and it slows the monster",
  ["mage-frost.s3.rarely1.if"] = "if another monster joins and you cannot cope",
  ["mage-frost.s3.rarely1.why"] = "a sheep does not attack",
  ["mage-frost.s4"] = "Dungeons, hard monsters and the first raid.",
  ["mage-frost.s4.alt.loop1.if"] = "if the pack reaches you",
  ["mage-frost.s4.alt.loop1.why"] = "it freezes them while you walk away",
  ["mage-frost.s4.alt.loop2.if"] = "if the pack is rooted and you can stand still",
  ["mage-frost.s4.alt.loop2.why"] = "it rains ice on the ground you chose",
  ["mage-frost.s4.alt.loop3.if"] = "if they are close enough to all be hit",
  ["mage-frost.s4.alt.loop3.why"] = "it hits everything in front of you and slows it",
  ["mage-frost.s4.alt.loop4.if"] = "if the last monster is close",
  ["mage-frost.s4.alt.loop4.why"] = "it hits everything around you",
  ["mage-frost.s4.alt.loop5.why"] = "it deals with a straggler",
  ["mage-frost.s4.alt.name"] = "A crowd of monsters",
  ["mage-frost.s4.alt.opening1.if"] = "before the pull",
  ["mage-frost.s4.alt.opening1.why"] = "it shields you while the pack closes in",
  ["mage-frost.s4.alt.say"] = "for a pack you can root with Frost Nova",
  ["mage-frost.s4.between1.if"] = "when it has run out",
  ["mage-frost.s4.between1.why"] = "more armour, and a slow on melee attackers",
  ["mage-frost.s4.between2.if"] = "when you have no drink left",
  ["mage-frost.s4.between2.why"] = "sitting with one brings mana back",
  ["mage-frost.s4.between3.if"] = "when you have no food left",
  ["mage-frost.s4.between3.why"] = "eating brings health back for no mana",
  ["mage-frost.s4.big"] = "Ice Block for the worst fight, Cold Snap for a second one",
  ["mage-frost.s4.loop1.if"] = "if a monster is casting a spell",
  ["mage-frost.s4.loop1.why"] = "it stops that school of spells for a while",
  ["mage-frost.s4.loop2.if"] = "if it has gone and the monster hits you",
  ["mage-frost.s4.loop2.why"] = "it shields you, and hits do not interrupt spells",
  ["mage-frost.s4.loop3.if"] = "if the monster reaches you",
  ["mage-frost.s4.loop3.why"] = "it freezes it, and you step back to cast",
  ["mage-frost.s4.loop4.if"] = "if the monster is frozen",
  ["mage-frost.s4.loop4.why"] = "spells crit far more often against a frozen monster",
  ["mage-frost.s4.loop5.if"] = "if the monster is nearly dead",
  ["mage-frost.s4.loop5.text"] = "Use your wand",
  ["mage-frost.s4.loop5.why"] = "it costs no mana, and your bar starts to refill",
  ["mage-frost.s4.loop6.why"] = "it is your main bolt, and it slows the monster",
  ["mage-frost.s4.low1.if"] = "if mana, not health, runs out first",
  ["mage-frost.s4.low1.why"] = "it keeps part of your mana regeneration while you cast",
  ["mage-frost.s4.low2.if"] = "when the bar is nearly empty",
  ["mage-frost.s4.low2.text"] = "Use your wand",
  ["mage-frost.s4.low2.why"] = "it costs no mana",
  ["mage-frost.s4.low3.if"] = "when the fight is over and the bar is empty",
  ["mage-frost.s4.low3.why"] = "it brings mana back much faster",
  ["mage-frost.s4.low4.if"] = "between fights, when the bar is low",
  ["mage-frost.s4.low4.text"] = "Sit and drink",
  ["mage-frost.s4.low4.why"] = "a full bar buys the next pulls",
  ["mage-frost.s4.opening1.if"] = "once, before the pull",
  ["mage-frost.s4.opening1.why"] = "more armour, and a slow on melee attackers",
  ["mage-frost.s4.opening2.if"] = "once, before the first pull",
  ["mage-frost.s4.opening2.why"] = "more Intellect means more mana to cast with",
  ["mage-frost.s4.opening3.if"] = "just before a hard pull",
  ["mage-frost.s4.opening3.why"] = "it shields you, and hits do not interrupt spells",
  ["mage-frost.s4.opening4.if"] = "from as far as you can reach",
  ["mage-frost.s4.opening4.why"] = "it is your main bolt, and it slows the monster",
  ["mage-frost.s4.rarely1.if"] = "if three or more monsters are on you",
  ["mage-frost.s4.rarely1.why"] = "it costs a lot of mana, so only for a crowd",
  ["mage-frost.split"] = "the last 17 points. This page takes Arcane for mana: Arcane Concentration gives free casts and Arcane Meditation lets mana come back while you cast. Some guides put them into Winter's Chill instead, for more Frost damage and less mana.",
  ["mage.advice.damage"] = "Frost. The safest way to level alone. A frozen or slowed monster hits you less. The price: Frost hits a little softer than Fire. Fire. The hardest hit. Fire has no slow, so Frostbolt and Frost Nova stay on the bar. The price: a monster that reaches you stays on you. Arcane. Mana and free spells. The price: most of the tree's damage arrives with Arcane Power at 40, so before then you level slower than the other two.",
  ["mage.ov.bad"] = "Being hit. You have little health and a cast that is interrupted is mana gone. Two monsters at once is the usual way a mage dies.",
  ["mage.ov.good"] = "Damage at range, and keeping monsters away: slows, freezes and a sheep. You make food and water for yourself and the group.",
  ["mage.ov.levelling"] = "Frostbolt from as far as you can reach, Frost Nova when it gets close, step back and cast again. Drink between pulls. Pull one monster at a time until you are sure.",
  ["mage.ov.resource"] = "Mana, and it is the whole game. Every cast spends it, so you cast, wait and drink. The wand costs nothing and finishes a fight while the bar refills.",
  ["mage.ov.ten"] = "You get your first talent point. Pick a build and Primer shows your first three picks. Frost is the safest way to level alone, and a respec costs gold.",
  ["mage.ov.who"] = "You hurt things from a distance with a cast bar and a mana bar. The craft is what to cast and when to stand still, and a monster that reaches you has won a round.",
  ["mage.role.damage"] = "Frost slows and freezes, so a monster hits you less. The price: it hits a little softer than Fire.",
  ["paladin"] = "A paladin keeps one seal, one aura and one blessing on each friend, and every one of them lasts a set time (a seal 30 seconds, a blessing 5 minutes). Mana runs the class. Retribution fights with a seal and Judgement, Holy heals, Protection holds. Every line below presses a button.",
  ["paladin-holy.intro"] = "Holy keeps people alive. The page cannot give a fixed order, because a healer's job is to answer whoever is losing health. It gives what each button is for, and when.",
  ["paladin-holy.line"] = "Heals the group. It levels slowly alone, and a dungeon wants it.",
  ["paladin-holy.note"] = "(31 points in Holy for Holy Shock, then 20 in Protection).",
  ["paladin-holy.p1"] = "10% more Intellect, so more mana and more heals.",
  ["paladin-holy.p10"] = "An instant heal on a friend, or damage on an enemy, every 30 seconds.",
  ["paladin-holy.p11"] = "Devotion Aura gives 25% more armour to the group.",
  ["paladin-holy.p12"] = "10% more armour from your gear.",
  ["paladin-holy.p13"] = "10 more Defense skill, so fewer hits land.",
  ["paladin-holy.p14"] = "The aura adds 15% to its effect, and the group resists silence and interrupt 15% more.",
  ["paladin-holy.p15"] = "Blessing of Protection comes back 2 minutes sooner.",
  ["paladin-holy.p2"] = "A heal keeps casting when you are hit (70% of the time), so you can heal mid-pull.",
  ["paladin-holy.p3"] = "12% more from Holy Light and Flash of Light.",
  ["paladin-holy.p4"] = "The cooldown drops from 1 hour to 40 minutes, and the target gets 30% more armour for 2 minutes. It opens the row for Illumination.",
  ["paladin-holy.p5"] = "After a critical heal you get back the mana the spell cost.",
  ["paladin-holy.p6"] = "Your next heal is a guaranteed critical, every 2 minutes. Use it on the big heal.",
  ["paladin-holy.p7"] = "Blessing of Wisdom is 20% stronger.",
  ["paladin-holy.p8"] = "10% more chance to resist fear and disorient. You take it to reach the next row.",
  ["paladin-holy.p9"] = "5% more critical chance on Holy spells.",
  ["paladin-holy.s1.opening"] = "Devotion Aura on, Blessing of Might, Seal of Righteousness, then hit. Judgement when it is ready, the seal again after it, Holy Light once the fight is over.",
  ["paladin-holy.s1.r1"] = "Put it on first. You and your party within 30 yards take less damage from every hit, until you change it.",
  ["paladin-holy.s1.r2"] = "Press it at the start of every pull. It lasts 30 seconds and adds Holy damage to each swing, and a slower weapon gets more out of it.",
  ["paladin-holy.s1.r3"] = "Whenever it is ready, every 10 seconds. It sets off the seal you wear, so put the seal back on after it.",
  ["paladin-holy.s1.r4"] = "Before the first pull and again when it ends. It adds attack power for 5 minutes, so it pays back over many fights.",
  ["paladin-holy.s1.r5"] = "Heal when nothing is hitting you. The cast takes 2.5 seconds and a hit can ruin it, so it belongs after the pull.",
  ["paladin-holy.s1.r6"] = "You swing 40% faster but each hit is weaker. Stay on Seal of Righteousness with a slow weapon, since the slower the weapon the more it adds.",
  ["paladin-holy.s1.r7"] = "You take nothing for 6 seconds but cannot attack, and it takes 5 minutes to come back. Keep it for the fight that would otherwise kill you.",
  ["paladin-holy.s1.r8"] = "A 3 second stun on a 1 minute cooldown. Press it to stop a monster running, or to buy the 2.5 seconds a Holy Light needs.",
  ["paladin-holy.s1.r9"] = "Removes 1 disease and 1 poison. Press it when a monster's sting is the thing wearing you down.",
  ["paladin-holy.s2"] = "A group, or one hurt friend. The page is a list of what each button is for.",
  ["paladin-holy.s2.r1"] = "The big heal. The cast takes 2.5 seconds, so use it only when the target will live that long.",
  ["paladin-holy.s2.r2"] = "On yourself and on the other casters. It gives 10 mana every 5 seconds for 5 minutes.",
  ["paladin-holy.s2.r3"] = "Keep it on. The group within 30 yards gets more armour, and it lasts until you change it.",
  ["paladin-holy.s2.r4"] = "6 seconds in which no physical attack reaches them, but they cannot fight either. 5 minutes to come back.",
  ["paladin-holy.s2.r5"] = "Removes one of each. Press it when it is the thing hurting someone.",
  ["paladin-holy.s2.r6"] = "Heals them for your full health and empties your mana. It takes 1 hour to come back, so save it for the moment.",
  ["paladin-holy.s3"] = "Dungeons.",
  ["paladin-holy.s3.r1"] = "A 1.5 second heal at a fraction of Holy Light's mana. Use it for most healing, and save Holy Light for the big hits.",
  ["paladin-holy.s3.r2"] = "The 2.5 second cast. Save it for the moment the tank is nearly gone, because the cast is long.",
  ["paladin-holy.s3.r3"] = "Your next heal is a critical. Use it on a Holy Light for the biggest heal you will get.",
  ["paladin-holy.s3.r4"] = "35% chance to ignore interrupts, for all in 30 yards. Swap Devotion Aura for it when casters get hit.",
  ["paladin-holy.s3.r5"] = "Your swing may return 50 mana, but a healer who swings is not healing. Use it only when standing idle.",
  ["paladin-holy.s3.r6"] = "On the casters, because mana is what runs out.",
  ["paladin-holy.s3.r7"] = "10 seconds with no slowing or rooting. The cooldown is 20 seconds, so use it when someone is stuck.",
  ["paladin-holy.s3.r8"] = "Brings them back with a little health and mana. Cannot be cast in combat.",
  ["paladin-holy.s4"] = "Dungeons and raids.",
  ["paladin-holy.s4.r1"] = "An instant heal on a 30 second cooldown. Use it when a hole is too sudden for a cast.",
  ["paladin-holy.s4.r2"] = "The main heal, because it costs little and casts in 1.5 seconds.",
  ["paladin-holy.s4.r3"] = "For the tank's worst moments. Cast Divine Favor first, so this heal is a critical.",
  ["paladin-holy.s4.r4"] = "Removes one of each. Use it before the next heal if the effect is the damage.",
  ["paladin-holy.s4.r5"] = "One blessing for every healer or caster of a class in the group. It saves buffing each player one by one.",
  ["paladin-holy.s4.r6"] = "Gives a friend 3 minutes of nothing hurting them, and it costs you your life. It takes 1 hour.",
  ["paladin-holy.split"] = "the last 20 points. A second road puts them in Retribution (Benediction, Improved Judgement, Conviction) for a healer who also fights alone. Your seals cost less and Judgement comes back sooner, and you give up the aura and the armour. This page takes Protection for the group.",
  ["paladin-protection.dry"] = "A monster still on you after 20 seconds means the job is working.",
  ["paladin-protection.intro"] = "Protection holds monsters on you and stays up. Threat is the list a monster keeps of who to hit next. The book has no taunt, so Righteous Fury, your seal and Holy Shield are what keep a monster looking at you.",
  ["paladin-protection.line"] = "Holds the monsters on you. The safest way to level, and the slowest.",
  ["paladin-protection.note"] = "(31 points in Protection for Holy Shield, then 20 in Holy).",
  ["paladin-protection.p1"] = "After a critical hit on you, 30% more block for 10 seconds or 5 blocks. It also opens Shield Specialization.",
  ["paladin-protection.p10"] = "10% more Intellect, which is mana for the next pull.",
  ["paladin-protection.p11"] = "15% more damage from Seal of Righteousness and its Judgement, which is threat.",
  ["paladin-protection.p12"] = "Holy damage on the ground around you for 8 seconds. This is your first area threat.",
  ["paladin-protection.p13"] = "12% more from Holy Light and Flash of Light.",
  ["paladin-protection.p14"] = "A heal keeps casting when you are hit (70% of the time), so you can heal mid-pull.",
  ["paladin-protection.p15"] = "The last point. Any talent you can reach would do as well.",
  ["paladin-protection.p2"] = "10% more armour from your gear.",
  ["paladin-protection.p3"] = "Righteous Fury gives 50% more threat, which is your whole job.",
  ["paladin-protection.p4"] = "10 more Defense skill, so fewer hits land and fewer are critical.",
  ["paladin-protection.p5"] = "3% more chance to hit, so Judgement and your seals land more.",
  ["paladin-protection.p6"] = "Less damage from every hit taken, and a block hurts the attacker. It opens Holy Shield.",
  ["paladin-protection.p7"] = "Your shield absorbs 30% more.",
  ["paladin-protection.p8"] = "10% more damage with a one-hander, which is threat.",
  ["paladin-protection.p9"] = "30% more block for 10 seconds and Holy damage for every block.",
  ["paladin-protection.s1.opening"] = "Devotion Aura on, Blessing of Might, Seal of Righteousness, then hit. Judgement when it is ready, the seal again after it, Holy Light once the fight is over.",
  ["paladin-protection.s1.r1"] = "Put it on first. You and your party within 30 yards take less damage from every hit, until you change it.",
  ["paladin-protection.s1.r2"] = "Press it at the start of every pull. It lasts 30 seconds and adds Holy damage to each swing, and a slower weapon gets more out of it.",
  ["paladin-protection.s1.r3"] = "Whenever it is ready, every 10 seconds. It sets off the seal you wear, so put the seal back on after it.",
  ["paladin-protection.s1.r4"] = "Before the first pull and again when it ends. It adds attack power for 5 minutes, so it pays back over many fights.",
  ["paladin-protection.s1.r5"] = "Heal when nothing is hitting you. The cast takes 2.5 seconds and a hit can ruin it, so it belongs after the pull.",
  ["paladin-protection.s1.r6"] = "You swing 40% faster but each hit is weaker. Stay on Seal of Righteousness with a slow weapon, since the slower the weapon the more it adds.",
  ["paladin-protection.s1.r7"] = "You take nothing for 6 seconds but cannot attack, and it takes 5 minutes to come back. Keep it for the fight that would otherwise kill you.",
  ["paladin-protection.s1.r8"] = "A 3 second stun on a 1 minute cooldown. Press it to stop a monster running, or to buy the 2.5 seconds a Holy Light needs.",
  ["paladin-protection.s1.r9"] = "Removes 1 disease and 1 poison. Press it when a monster's sting is the thing wearing you down.",
  ["paladin-protection.s2"] = "A shield, a group. The tree opens at 10.",
  ["paladin-protection.s2.opening"] = "Devotion Aura, Righteous Fury (from 16), Seal of Righteousness, then hit.",
  ["paladin-protection.s2.r1"] = "Turn it on. Your Holy attacks draw 60% more attention, and it lasts 30 minutes, so once an outing is enough.",
  ["paladin-protection.s2.r2"] = "On before the first hit. It adds Holy damage to each swing, and Righteous Fury makes that damage count as threat.",
  ["paladin-protection.s2.r3"] = "Every 10 seconds, because it is damage and so threat.",
  ["paladin-protection.s2.r4"] = "The group within 30 yards takes less from each hit.",
  ["paladin-protection.s2.r5"] = "A 3 second stun. Use it on the one that went for the healer.",
  ["paladin-protection.s2.r6"] = "Heal when nothing is hitting you, because the cast takes 2.5 seconds.",
  ["paladin-protection.s3"] = "Dungeons, groups of monsters.",
  ["paladin-protection.s3.r1"] = "On before the pull. Your Holy attacks draw 60% more attention.",
  ["paladin-protection.s3.r2"] = "Your seal. Seal of Command is not yours until you take the Retribution road.",
  ["paladin-protection.s3.r3"] = "Every 10 seconds on the monster you are holding, because it is damage and so threat.",
  ["paladin-protection.s3.r4"] = "Stuns it for 4 seconds at rank 2. 1 minute to come back.",
  ["paladin-protection.s3.r5"] = "On yourself before the pull. Less damage from each hit, and a blocked attacker takes Holy damage.",
  ["paladin-protection.s3.r6"] = "Pulls the damage off them for 8 seconds at rank 2, but they cannot fight. 5 minutes to come back.",
  ["paladin-protection.s3.r7"] = "The group is less likely to be interrupted while hit.",
  ["paladin-protection.s3.r8"] = "8 seconds with nothing hurting you, but you cannot attack. 5 minutes to come back.",
  ["paladin-protection.s4"] = "Dungeons and raids.",
  ["paladin-protection.s4.opening"] = "Righteous Fury, Holy Shield, Seal of Righteousness, Judgement. The first move on a pack is Consecration, from 51.",
  ["paladin-protection.s4.r1"] = "Keep it up. It lasts 10 seconds and returns in 10, so it can cover the whole fight, adding block, Holy damage per block and 20% more threat.",
  ["paladin-protection.s4.r2"] = "Keep it on. It is the damage that Righteous Fury makes threat.",
  ["paladin-protection.s4.r3"] = "Every 10 seconds, because it is damage and so threat.",
  ["paladin-protection.s4.r4"] = "8 seconds of Holy damage around you. Stand where the pack stands.",
  ["paladin-protection.s4.r5"] = "5 seconds of stun on a 1 minute cooldown. Use it on the one that is the problem.",
  ["paladin-protection.s4.r6"] = "Keep it on yourself, because every hit taken is a little smaller.",
  ["paladin-protection.s4.r7"] = "10 seconds with nothing hurting you, but your attacks come half as often. 5 minutes to come back.",
  ["paladin-protection.split"] = "the last 20 points. A second road puts them in Retribution (Benediction, Deflection, Conviction, Improved Judgement, Vindication) for more parry and more critical hits. This page takes Holy because Consecration is the only way a paladin holds a pack, and the price is parry and critical chance.",
  ["paladin-retribution.dry"] = "Most of this page waits on Judgement. If it is not ready, hit the monster.",
  ["paladin-retribution.hc1"] = "Judgement, seal, swing. Do not pull five monsters at once without your cooldowns ready.",
  ["paladin-retribution.hc2"] = "Divine Shield is your escape from level 34. When a fight has gone wrong, press it, then heal or walk away.",
  ["paladin-retribution.hc3"] = "Keep a shield in your bags and put it on when you run from a hard hitter.",
  ["paladin-retribution.hc4"] = "Never run out of mana in a fight. Without it you have no heal and no Judgement.",
  ["paladin-retribution.hcwhy"] = "On a Hardcore realm this is the safer road. The other road trades that safety for damage.",
  ["paladin-retribution.intro"] = "Retribution fights in melee with one big weapon and a seal that adds to every swing. It is the paladin that kills alone. The rest of the page is about which seal, and when to spend it with Judgement.",
  ["paladin-retribution.line"] = "One big weapon, a seal and Judgement. It kills alone, and most players level this way.",
  ["paladin-retribution.note"] = "(31 points or more in Retribution for Repentance. The rest are Holy, and Protection on the Holy-first road.)",
  ["paladin-retribution.p1"] = "Judgement and your seals cost less mana, and mana is what stops a paladin.",
  ["paladin-retribution.p10"] = "Blessing of Might gives a little more attack power. A spare point until the next row opens.",
  ["paladin-retribution.p11"] = "After a critical hit you deal more Physical and Holy damage for a few seconds.",
  ["paladin-retribution.p12"] = "A stun for a humanoid that heals itself. It is the last talent of the tree.",
  ["paladin-retribution.p13"] = "More Strength. The Holy block is where the last points go.",
  ["paladin-retribution.p14"] = "Seal of Righteousness and its Judgement do more damage.",
  ["paladin-retribution.p15"] = "The last point of Improved Seal of Righteousness.",
  ["paladin-retribution.p16"] = "Holy damage on the ground beneath you, for packs. It costs a lot of mana.",
  ["paladin-retribution.p17"] = "Holy Light and Flash of Light heal for more.",
  ["paladin-retribution.p18"] = "The rest of Improved Blessing of Might.",
  ["paladin-retribution.p19"] = "Lay on Hands comes back much sooner. The last two points are a matter of taste.",
  ["paladin-retribution.p2"] = "Judgement comes back sooner, so you press it more often.",
  ["paladin-retribution.p3"] = "More of the attacks on you are parried.",
  ["paladin-retribution.p4"] = "You run faster, and the points cost you nothing you needed.",
  ["paladin-retribution.p5"] = "Your seal if your weapon is slow: each swing may add Holy damage. It is a talent, not a trainer spell.",
  ["paladin-retribution.p6"] = "More critical hits, and Vengeance needs all five.",
  ["paladin-retribution.p7"] = "Back to Deflection while the next row opens.",
  ["paladin-retribution.p8"] = "An aura that makes your party's Holy damage hit harder. One point, for a group.",
  ["paladin-retribution.p9"] = "More damage with a two-handed weapon, which is the reason for the weapon.",
  ["paladin-retribution.r2.p1"] = "More Intellect is a bigger mana pool, and a paladin who runs dry stops fighting.",
  ["paladin-retribution.r2.p10"] = "More damage with a two-handed weapon, which is the weapon this build is for.",
  ["paladin-retribution.r2.p11"] = "Judgement and your seals cost less mana, so you press them more often before you need to drink.",
  ["paladin-retribution.r2.p12"] = "After a critical hit you deal more Physical and Holy damage for a few seconds. With Conviction behind it, it comes up often.",
  ["paladin-retribution.r2.p13"] = "It does nothing without a shield, but its five points open Precision on the next row.",
  ["paladin-retribution.r2.p14"] = "More chance to hit with melee weapons, so fewer swings are wasted.",
  ["paladin-retribution.r2.p15"] = "Blessing of Protection comes back sooner and Blessing of Freedom lasts longer: two escapes you will want in a hard pull.",
  ["paladin-retribution.r2.p16"] = "The last point goes to Repentance, the tree's deepest talent: it puts a humanoid out of the fight for up to six seconds, until something hits it.",
  ["paladin-retribution.r2.p2"] = "Your heals are less likely to be spoiled when something hits you mid-cast. You will heal yourself in the middle of fights, so this keeps them landing.",
  ["paladin-retribution.r2.p3"] = "Blessing of Might gives more attack power, and you wear it every fight, so every swing gets the bonus.",
  ["paladin-retribution.r2.p4"] = "More of the blows aimed at you are parried and never land, which is a cheap way to take less damage.",
  ["paladin-retribution.r2.p5"] = "Your Seal of Command at last: its first rank is a talent, not something a trainer sells. Each swing may add Holy damage, and a slow weapon adds the most.",
  ["paladin-retribution.r2.p6"] = "You run faster, which a levelling paladin uses all day. The points also open the row of talents below.",
  ["paladin-retribution.r2.p7"] = "More chance to land a critical hit, which is where a two-hander's big numbers come from.",
  ["paladin-retribution.r2.p8"] = "The aura that hurts monsters hitting you hurts them more. They hit you all fight, so it pays back each time.",
  ["paladin-retribution.r2.p9"] = "The rest of Conviction: more critical hits, and Vengeance further down will not open without all five.",
  ["paladin-retribution.roadwhy"] = "Most guides take this road. The other road trades Seal of Command until level 30 and early damage for mana and heals a hit does not spoil.",
  ["paladin-retribution.s1.between1.if"] = "when nothing is hitting you and you are hurt",
  ["paladin-retribution.s1.between1.why"] = "the cast is slow, and about 80 percent is enough",
